The site is linc.cis.upenn.edu in the directory pub/NH3.0.
Make sure you transfer the binary files by typing the word
"binary" before you transfer them or they'll be messed
up.  If my memory serves me right, when you are in the NH3.0
directory you then have to choose which subdirectory you want
the files from (according to which machine you want it on):

  /amiga
  /atari
  /mac
  /os2
  /PC

These are the five choices I think.  There are about 4 or 5
files in all (at least there was for the PC), two of which
are binary (.exe extensions), and the others are either ASCII
help files or batch (.bat) files.

*No* compilation is necessary.  The program loads itself with 
the batch file (read the README doc after downloading it).

P.S. Last time I looked it was the latest 3.09 version.  There
is no 4.0 version yet.

